From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [TEST PATCH] server: Report the service manager in session zero.

AI-assisted (Codex); LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted upstream.
Based on the session-reporting experiment by Lorenzo Cozzaglio in
lori28167/autocad-wine-linux, commit ec02824ab92c548202636d889e94f3ea14e9ff85.

The Winum AutoCAD reference reports services.exe in session 1 and the
registered Autodesk service times out while connecting to the service
manager. Go's Windows service detection reads the parent's session
from the process list. Test the effect of reporting services.exe in
session 0 there. This diagnostic candidate leaves tokens and the
service's actual session unchanged. Windows process-list measurement
and the AutoCAD service-start comparison are pending.

diff --git a/server/process.c b/server/process.c
--- a/server/process.c
+++ b/server/process.c
@@ -1986,6 +1986,19 @@
     }
 }

+/* Scope the service-manager session experiment to process enumeration. */
+static unsigned int reported_process_session( const struct process *process )
+{
+    static const WCHAR suffix[] = {'\\','s','e','r','v','i','c','e','s','.','e','x','e'};
+    const size_t len = sizeof(suffix);
+
+    if (process->image && process->imagelen >= len &&
+        !memicmp_strW( process->image + (process->imagelen - len) / sizeof(WCHAR), suffix, len ))
+        return 0;
+
+    return process->session_id;
+}
+
 /* Get a list of processes and threads currently running */
 DECL_HANDLER(list_processes)
 {
@@ -2044,7 +2057,7 @@
         process_info->priority = process->priority;
         process_info->pid = process->id;
         process_info->parent_pid = process->parent_id;
-        process_info->session_id = process->session_id;
+        process_info->session_id = reported_process_session( process );
         process_info->handle_count = get_handle_table_count(process);
         process_info->unix_pid = process->unix_pid;
         pos += sizeof(*process_info);
